        "comments": "The assembly aLisMon1.hap1.1 is based on 30x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Programme (https://www.sanger.ac.uk/programme/tree-of-life/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Haplotypic inversion detected on the following consecutive regions: Chromosome_1_HAP1_1 from 1049.68 Mbp to 1391.63 Mbp and Chromosome_1_HAP1_2 from 0 Mbp to 94.57 Mbp. The respective consecutive regions on HAP2 are: Chromosome_1_HAP2_1 from 1124.84 Mbp to 1388.88 Mbp and on Chromosome_1_HAP2_2 from 0 Mbp - 102.43 Mbp. As some chromosomes are larger than 2 Gbp in length they were split in parts 1 and 2.",
